#{[17592186400750 "Let $\\mathbf{u}=⟨4,5,-1⟩$ and $\\mathbf{v}=⟨-6,0,2⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{u}\\times \\mathbf{v}.$"] [17592186401226 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}yz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-x+y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$${∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186401233 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}z,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$${∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186401240 "For a surface $S$ given by $y=2x{z}^{3}$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\hspace{0.222em}Q,\\hspace{0.222em}R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{D}(\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\hspace{0.167em}{z}^{3}+Q-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\hspace{0.167em}x{z}^{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $\\mathbf{j}$-component.*"] [17592186401247 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\hspace{0.222em}Q,\\hspace{0.222em}R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{∂x}-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}+R)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?"] [17592186401254 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\hspace{0.222em}Q,\\hspace{0.222em}R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}-Q\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}+R)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?"] [17592186401261 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨\\frac{1}{z},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{xy}{z},\\hspace{0.222em}z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x-y}$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le x.$"] [17592186401275 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+2w \\\\ v-u \\\\ uw\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186401282 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{u} \\\\ {e}^{u+w} \\\\ uv+w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186401302 "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le x+3y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le z-3y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+3y,\\,v=z-3y,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{cos}^{2}⁡(x+z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(z-3y)\\,dV={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$"] [17592186401336 "Let $C$ be the intersection of the surface $z=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}$ and the boundary of the infinite vertical column enclosed by the planes $x=\\pm 1,$ and $y=\\pm 1.$ Given that the curve $C$ is oriented counter-clockwise when viewed from above and $\\text{curl}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{F}=⟨x,\\hspace{0.222em}y,\\hspace{0.222em}-2z⟩,$ the circulation of $\\mathbf{F}$ along $C$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\n$$"] [17592186401357 "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2x{y}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}?$"] [17592186403475 "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z,\n$$ find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [17592186403571 "At which points on the curve ${y}^{2}-4xy=-5{x}^{2}+1$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{i}?$"] [17592186406696 "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=2x{y}^{3}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+({x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2yz)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z).$"] [17592186406697 "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f=\\mathbf{F},$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{sin}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}y+3{y}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186406698 "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(2x+y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(2y+x+z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(y-2z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$"] [17592186406699 "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(\\operatorname{sin}y+y)\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+(x\\operatorname{cos}y+x)\\text{ }\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186406700 "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f=\\mathbf{F},$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=2xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({x}^{2}+3{y}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186406771 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+vw \\\\ {v}^{2} \\\\ w+v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186406772 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+vw,\\,y=2-uv,\\,z={v}^{2}-w.\n$$"] [17592186407632 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}=\\operatorname{cos}\\pi x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+y\\operatorname{sin}\\pi y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+{e}^{2z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$ \nEvaluate $\\mathrm{∇}\\cdot \\mathbf{F}$ at the point $(0,1,0).$"] [17592186407846 "Determine $\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{3}-xy}{{x}^{3}y}.$"] [17592186407847 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186407848 "$\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (2,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{xy+2}-2}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4}=$"] [17592186407849 "$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{y+z}{\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z}}=\n$$"] [17592186408071 "Let $\\mathbf{r}=⟨-4,-1,2⟩$, $\\mathbf{q}=⟨-2,3,1⟩$ and $\\mathbf{p}=⟨5,-2,-1⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{r}\\cdot (\\mathbf{q}\\times \\mathbf{p})$ using a determinant.\n\n$\\mathbf{r}\\cdot (\\mathbf{q}\\times \\mathbf{p})=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186408111 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨-2,2,-3⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨2,-1,2⟩$ and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨-2,1,1⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c}).$"] [17592186408112 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨-1,2,4⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨0,3,1⟩$ and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨2,5,0⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})$ using a determinant.\n\n$\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186409609 "Given that $$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\