.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}.$*"] [17592186419785 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨1,-3,0⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-2,2,0⟩$ and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨2,0,-4⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})$ using a determinant.\n\n$\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186419786 "Find $\\mathbf{b}\\cdot (\\mathbf{c}\\times \\mathbf{a})$, if $-5\\mathbf{a}\\cdot ((6\\mathbf{b})\\times (4\\mathbf{c}))=120.$\n\n$\\mathbf{b}\\cdot (\\mathbf{c}\\times \\mathbf{a})=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186419787 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨-2,0,-1⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-3,-1,4⟩$ and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨5,-2,-2⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})$ using a determinant.\n\n$\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186420301 "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+10\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$"] [17592186420302 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=10\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+5\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $b(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*"] [17592186420303 "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=7\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+11\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2